From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 "this Mac" passkeys: list and delete for the host's settings (ABI 1.72)

Engine side of docs/FEATURE-SPECS/PASSKEYS-AND-SITE-PERMISSIONS.md, 1.7
(security review PK-07). A passkey made on "this Mac" is a Secure Enclave key
whose keychain item carries the site and the account sealed with the
profile's metadata secret (device/fido/mac/credential_store.h). Nobody could
see or remove one from Darni: Chromium's page for them
(chrome://settings/passkeys) is not reachable from the host's settings, and
the host cannot read the sealed names by itself.

ReArcProfileGetLocalPasskeys answers for a profile with one JSON object:
"available" (the app is signed with the profile authenticator's keychain
access group) and "passkeys", each with its credential ID in hex, the site
(the relying party's ID) and the account's two names. It is
LocalCredentialManagement::Enumerate, the call behind Chromium's own page,
so the order and the content are Chromium's. Reading asks for no Touch ID.

ReArcProfileDeleteLocalPasskey deletes one for good and answers with the list
as it is afterwards. TouchIdCredentialStore::DeleteCredentialById removes a
keychain item by its credential ID alone, anywhere in the access group, so
the bridge first lists the profile's own passkeys and deletes only an ID it
finds there: an ID of another profile, or a guess, is not_found and reaches
no SecItemDelete.

Without the access group in the signature (a build without it, a C ABI test
host, a development bundle) "available" is false, the list is empty, delete
is unsupported, and nothing touches the keychain or the profile's metadata
secret.

A release bundle in verification mode never has the profile authenticator
(security advance read 2026-11-24, point 5). The copies the release scripts
run their gates on, --qa bundles and the upgrade checks' copies of a previous
release are signed by the same team and may be started on a copy of a
person's profile; with the group they could use, list and delete that
person's real passkeys. rearc::WebAuthnKeychainAccessGroup() (tab/097) now
gives such a bundle (ReArcReleaseVerification true in the main bundle's
Info.plist) a group name no build is ever signed with, so Chromium's own
check (TouchIdContext::TouchIdAvailable) finds the authenticator unavailable
for requests, and this patch's calls report "available": false. The release
scripts also sign those copies without the group; this holds if one slips
through.

Private profiles are unsupported (they use their original profile's
passkeys). The site chose the account names: the host treats them as
untrusted text. Nothing is logged by the engine.

No test in the tree creates a passkey: the store's fakes are test-only
targets (crypto:test_support), so the engine has none. engine/tests/
c_abi_local_passkeys_host.mm runs the calls on a host without the group
(available false, delete unsupported, the argument checks, a private
profile); the list and delete logic with content is tested in the shell with
an injected store.

Touches: chrome/app/framework.exports, chrome/app/framework.order,
chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/{rearc_engine_abi.h,
rearc_engine_abi.mm, rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm, rearc_local_passkeys.cc
(new), rearc_webauthn.cc, rearc_webauthn.h}. No Chromium file outside the
bridge.

Bridge 0.86.0, ABI 1.72, feature local_passkeys. One callback type added
(ReArcLocalPasskeysCallback, the shape of ReArcSitePermissionsCallback), no
struct. The header's minor version stays 73: tab/105 (ABI 1.73) is under
this patch in the overlay, so the order in the series is 103, 105, 104.

Built into the release engine on 2026-11-25 (overlay faf0faf7a4 on
577e70cef2, out/ReArc-codecs-arm64): the framework exports the two
functions, engine/tests/check_abi172_imports.py passes, and
c_abi_local_passkeys_host.mm passes on that engine with every connection on
loopback. Not run: a build signed with the group (no test may reach a real
passkey), so the list with content and a real delete are unexercised in the
engine.

Last rebased: 2026-11-25 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.114 (overlay 577e70cef2,
through tab/103 and tab/105).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

