+// "This Mac" passkeys (local_passkeys, ABI 1.72): the passkeys Chromium's
+// profile authenticator keeps for a profile, for a list in the host's
+// settings with a way to delete one. They are what a request's "this_mac"
+// way makes: a key in the Secure Enclave, in the keychain access group
+// <team>.<bundle identifier>.webauthn of the signed app, with the site and
+// the account sealed by a secret in the profile's preferences. One belongs to
+// one profile on one Mac and is in no sync. The engine is asked because only
+// it can read the sealed names; it is Chromium's own page for them
+// (chrome://settings/passkeys, LocalCredentialManagement) without the page.
+//
+// json is a UTF-8 object; a host ignores keys it does not know:
+//   "available": the app is signed with the access group, so this profile
+//     can have such passkeys. false: no passkeys, and the engine asked the
+//     keychain nothing and wrote nothing (a build without the group, a test
+//     host, and every bundle in release verification mode, which names a
+//     group no build is signed with: such a bundle never reaches a real
+//     passkey).
+//   "passkeys": this profile's, in Chromium's order (by site, then account).
+//     "id": the credential's ID, lower-case hex, for
+//     ReArcProfileDeleteLocalPasskey; "rp_id": the site it signs in to (the
+//     relying party's ID, a domain); "user_name" and "user_display_name": the
+//     account as the site named it when the passkey was made, either may be
+//     "". The site chose both names: a host treats them as untrusted text.
+// Reading asks for no Touch ID and no password. Snapshot at call time,
+// delivered deferred, exactly once, borrowed. An unknown profile:
+// profile_not_found. A private profile: unsupported (it uses its original
+// profile's passkeys and has none of its own). A null completion:
+// invalid_argument. The keychain refused the query: the completion gets
+// internal with "passkeys": [].
+typedef void (*ReArcLocalPasskeysCallback)(void* context,
+                                           ReArcStatus status,
+                                           uint64_t profile_id,
+                                           const char* json);
+REARC_ENGINE_EXPORT ReArcStatus ReArcProfileGetLocalPasskeys(
+    uint64_t profile_id, ReArcLocalPasskeysCallback completion, void* context);
+// Deletes one passkey of the profile for good: the keychain item and its key
+// in the Secure Enclave. There is no undo and no copy anywhere; the site
+// keeps its half and will no longer be answered by this Mac. The host asks
+// the person first. credential_id: an "id" of the profile's list. Only a
+// passkey of this profile's own list is deleted, so an ID of another profile
+// or a guess removes nothing: the completion gets not_found. The completion
+// always carries the list as it is afterwards: ok when the passkey is gone,
+// not_found, or internal when the keychain refused. Returned at once, and
+// then no completion: invalid_argument (null, not hex, empty, over 1024
+// bytes), profile_not_found, unsupported (a private profile, or "available"
+// is false).
+REARC_ENGINE_EXPORT ReArcStatus ReArcProfileDeleteLocalPasskey(
+    uint64_t profile_id,
+    const char* credential_id,
+    ReArcLocalPasskeysCallback completion,
+    void* context);
+
 // Blocked hosts (content_blocking_hosts, ABI 1.69): what ReArcTabGetBlockedCount
 // counts, by site, for a "Blocked on this page" list. *json is +1 malloc,
 // NUL-terminated UTF-8; free with ReArcBufferFree.
